# Step 9 — Check `last`

After you've performed the tests, run:

```bash
last -F | head -20
```

This is useful because `last` reconstructs login sessions from the system's login accounting information.

You might see:

```text
userid    pts/0    10.x.x.x    Thu Aug 13 21:10:12 2026   still logged in
userid    pts/0    10.x.x.x    Thu Aug 13 20:50:32 2026 - 21:05:10
```

But don't make `last` our final source yet. We need to see what happens with DCV and reconnects.

